  {"id":"gramin","name":"Gramin","city":"Bengaluru","area":"Koramangala","lat":12.93446,"lng":77.61343,"rating":4.3,"reviews":11824,"price":"₹400–600","cuisine":"North Indian","type":"meal","note":"One of Bangalore's original vegetarian restaurants, with an excellent Jain menu. The Gujarati owner loves food and has kept the standard up for years. Try the mirchi ka salan, the sweet karela starter and the Rajasthani kurkure bhindi. They've helped us with food for Ekadashi fasts too."},
  {"id":"kesariya-north","name":"Kesariya","city":"Bengaluru","area":"Sadashivanagar","lat":13.0051,"lng":77.58387,"rating":4.1,"reviews":1654,"price":"₹600–800","cuisine":"Rajasthani thali","type":"meal","note":"I've been a couple of times. Good, and like the JP Nagar Kesariya, though that one is much better."},
  {"id":"kesariya-south","name":"Kesariya","city":"Bengaluru","area":"JP Nagar 2nd Phase","lat":12.90658,"lng":77.58962,"rating":4,"reviews":4457,"price":"₹600–800","cuisine":"Rajasthani thali","type":"meal","note":"Closest to our hearts, thanks to Kishore, who was a captain at ISKCON Bangalore and then here. The chef taught us gravies without onion and garlic that we still make at home, and they can make the whole buffet without them. Things may have changed, but with the same chef it's the top buffet."},
  {"id":"kapoors-cafe","name":"Kapoor's Cafe","city":"Bengaluru","area":"Jayanagar","lat":12.93274,"lng":77.58507,"rating":4.2,"reviews":10810,"price":"₹200–1,000","cuisine":"Punjabi","type":"meal","note":"Top. A paratha the size of a pizza with lots of butter, sarson ka saag and makki ki roti, all without onion and garlic. The kadhi chawal is good too. Amazing place."},
  {"id":"kailash-parbat-jayanagar","name":"Kailash Parbat","city":"Bengaluru","area":"Jayanagar","lat":12.93395,"lng":77.58261,"rating":4.1,"reviews":4348,"price":"₹200–1,200","cuisine":"North Indian","type":"meal","note":"Same great food as the other Kailash Parbats, but more upscale. Omkar, the captain here, used to be a captain at Rajdhani in Malleshwaram, the first Rajdhani I went to."},
